<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Đồng Khánh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1864">1864</a>–<a href="/years/1889">1889</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Dong Khanh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Đồng Khánh was emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> of the Nguyen dynasty from 1885 to 1889. After the regent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ton-that-thuyet">Tôn Thất Thuyết</a> fled from Huế with the young emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ham-nghi">Hàm Nghi</a> to lead the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/can-vuong">Cần Vương</a> resistance, the French placed Hàm Nghi's elder brother on the throne. He cooperated with the French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> and urged the rebels to submit, and he died after a short reign.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dong-khanh.jpg" alt="Đồng Khánh" width="320" height="456" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tonkin11h.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Early life and background</h2><p>Đồng Khánh was born Nguyễn Phúc Ưng Kỷ on 19 February 1864 in the Imperial City of Huế. His childhood name, Chánh Mông, came from the Chánh Mông palace where he was raised. He was the eldest son of Prince Nguyễn Phúc Hồng Cai, a son of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thieu-tri">Thiệu Trị</a>, and his concubine Bùi Thị Thanh. His uncle, Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tu-duc">Tự Đức</a>, had no children, so he was adopted and given the title Kiên Giang quận công, Duke of Kiên Giang.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Reign</h2><p>After French armies captured Huế and the Imperial City fell, the court regents Nguyễn Văn Tường and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ton-that-thuyet">Tôn Thất Thuyết</a> took the young Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ham-nghi">Hàm Nghi</a> out of the Purple Forbidden City. They brought him to Tân Sở in the mountains as the figurehead of a movement against the French. To take away Hàm Nghi's legitimacy, General de Courcy and the résident de Champeaux asked the empress dowager Nghi Thiên to enthrone his elder half brother. With the backing of the governor of Annam, Prince Nguyễn Phúc Ưng Kỷ was crowned as the ninth emperor of Đại Nam on 19 September 1885 and took the era name Đồng Khánh.</p><p>Đồng Khánh was pro-French. According to the later historian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tran-trong-kim">Trần Trọng Kim</a>, he had a gentle personality, loved luxurious jewellery and adopted French culture, so the colonial government favoured him. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ham-nghi">Hàm Nghi</a> fled to Quảng Bình, Đồng Khánh agreed to the French request to travel there and persuade Hàm Nghi and his loyal followers to surrender, but he was unsuccessful. Hàm Nghi was later betrayed by his follower Trương Quang Ngọc, captured by the French and exiled to Algérie.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Death and legacy</h2><p>Đồng Khánh died on 28 January 1889 at the age of 24 and was given the temple name Cảnh Tông. His son, Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khai-dinh">Khải Định</a>, granted him a longer posthumous name in 1916. He was buried in the Tư Lăng mausoleum at Dương Xuân Thượng village, Hương Thuỷ commune, in Thừa Thiên Province.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Đồng Khánh” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Huế, in what is now <a href="/countries/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. Died in Huế, in what is now <a href="/countries/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=16.46,107.58&amp;year=1880" aria-label="Huế on the atlas"><svg class="map map-globe map-loc" viewBox="0 0 10000 10000" role="img" aria-label="Globe: the birthplace of Đồng Khánh"><image href="/maps/globes/g120n30.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="10000"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3989 6093h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3989 6093h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=16.46,107.58&amp;year=1880">What was here in 1880? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
